WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.704
Well meet Kate, I know
you know Dr. Goodall.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.006
Y'all have met obviously, right?

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.107
- We met, yes.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:08.808
- I was gonna say that would
be weird at this point.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.244
So I heard that you just turned 11, right?

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.078
- [Ava] Yes.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.146
- Happy Birthday.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:13.980
- Thank you.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.814
- [Kelly] That's so exciting.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:15.648
What'd you do? Have a party?

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.784
- Yeah, I hung out with
my friends and family

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.886
and I love all the presents I got.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.954
- [Kelly] Awesome.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.288
- I got a big Squish
Mellow. I really love that.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.223
- [Kelly] Oh my God, my daughter

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.891
is obsessed with Squish Mellows.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.393
- Yeah.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.495
- And I went to my favorite
place ever, Canada's Wonderland.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.096
It's an amusement park.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.898
And I love roller coasters so much-

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:32.732
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.566
- so that was really fun.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.035
- Do you like when your stomach
gets taken away from you?

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:35.869
- [Ava] Yeah.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.037
- Me too.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:40.440
It changes a little as you get older.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.908
You're like, huh, I can't do the ride

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.576
over and over again anymore.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.545
I could do it once, but it's really fun.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.414
So you got to travel around the world

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.049
when you were working on the show Jane.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.817
So did you have a favorite?

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:54.087
- Yes. I went to Kenya,
which is my favorite.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.888
- [Kelly] Beautiful.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.390
- And I really loved
it because I got to see

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.093
a lion family and they had
two little cubs that were

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:03.430
actually eating the insides of a zebra.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.365
So I thought that was amazing.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.366
- [Kelly] Were you scared at all?

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.201
'Cause they get really close.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.669
- No, I wasn't scared.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.503
- [Kelly] Love it.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:11.604
- I just love them.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.274
- Yeah, me too, so pretty and beautiful.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.509
So Dr. Jane, how much
joy does it bring you

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:20.447
to see kids like Ava
Louise inspired by animals?

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:23.817
- Well, I want all, everybody
inspired, not just kids.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.617
- [Kelly] Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.320
- Everybody should understand
that animals have feelings

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.790
emotions, personalities and intelligence.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.858
You know that, don't you?

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:32.692
- Yeah.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.461
- And are affected by what we do.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:35.495
- Absolutely.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.329
- [Kelly] Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.497
- Well, we're destroying them.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:40.467
And so that's why a show
like this is so important

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.302
because it'll help other children

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:45.672
to realize animals need help, right?

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.507
- Absolutely. Well Kate,

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:50.477
what animals have fascinated
your kids the most?

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:53.213
Like which ones do they
go nuts anywhere they are?

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.581
I bet chimpanzees at this point.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.816
- Yes. They know 'cause of my obsession.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:02:00.019
That sort of has forced
them to be obsessed.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.156
But my husband has this thing about

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.226
naming each of us as an animal.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:08.428
So he thinks that I'm a snow fox.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.262
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.697
- For whatever reason-

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.031
- You a little sneaky?

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.700
- and the big, Oh, is
that why he thinks that?

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:14.968
- I don't know, are you sneaky?

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:15.802
You're sly.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.903
- I'll never say.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:17.904
- [Kelly] Okay, okay.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.873
- So yeah, we like foxes
in our family a lot.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:20.707
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.176
- I always Red admiral in my group.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.378
We all had to choose our animal names and

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:29.015
as I was the oldest, I was,
admiral was what attracted me.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.383
Red Admiral Butterfly.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.217
- I love it.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.786
- I love it. So, Dr.
Jane, could you tell us

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.822
a little about the new show, Jane?

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.558
- Well, I think this Jane can tell more

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.859
about the show than I can.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:45.798
but basically, in the
show, I'm your hero, right?

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:46.966
- [Ava] Yes.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:50.136
- In the show, probably not
really, but in the show.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.239
So you have a room and it's
got all sorts of decorations

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:56.142
of pictures of Jane and
David Graybeard and-

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:56.976
- [Ava] Yes.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.978
- everything. And so, yeah.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.748
- Oh, so she's your inspiration
that puts you on a course-

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:02.582
- [Ava] Yeah.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.783
- Right? That's amazing.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.185
What all do you get to do in the show?

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.386
Like where do you go? What do you do?

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.621
Do you become a bee? Is
that what I'm seeing?

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:14.394
- So Jane basically goes
on like imaginary missions

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.828
with her best friend David

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.697
and her toy chimpanzee, Graybeard,

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.666
which comes to life.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.602
And basically she does different things

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:26.072
like she rides on bees
and on those missions,

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.576
she finds lots of cool animal facts

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.944
and how to save the animal.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.614
- And I'm assuming pollen
and how we need bees.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.448
- Yeah.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.282
- All of that kind of stuff.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.116
I love that.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.518
Like I love watching,
I love when people come

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.119
out with shows where parents can sit

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.155
with them and we enjoy it as much

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.657
as our kids do and we enjoy
like learning with them.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.859
'Cause some of the things you
learn when you're in school

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.595
and then you forget when
you're older and you're like

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.930
I remember that from
like sixth grade science.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.198
And you're like, wait

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.968
I'm not smarter than a
fifth grader apparently.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.303
But Dr. Jane, what's the
most important message

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.606
that you wanna share with
people about our world?

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:01.274
What do you think the
most important thing is?

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:04.210
- I think the most important
thing is to remember

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:08.881
that every day we live on
this planet, we make an impact

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.951
and we get to choose what
sort of impact we make.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:14.120
But in order to be able to choose

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.955
we have to alleviate poverty,

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.156
because if you are really poor

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.659
you can't choose as we all can.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:20.893
You know, don't buy that

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.062
because it was bad for the environment

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:28.034
or cruel to animals or cheap
because of unfair wages.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:31.571
That's really important, isn't it?

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:32.538
- Yes.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.840
- Everything is connected.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:37.143
Well let's do a quick
commercial break everybody.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.611
Y'all be sure to watch Jane.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.580
You can find it on Apple TV+.

